{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q413611","formula":"C₇H₅KO₂","hill":"C7H5KO2","elements":["H","C","O","K"],"composition":{"C":7.0,"H":5.0,"K":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Potassium benzoate","ru":"Бензоат калия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Potassium benzoate (E212), the potassium salt of benzoic acid with the formula C6H5COOK, is a food preservative that inhibits the growth of mold, yeast and some bacteria. It works best in low-pH products, below 4.5, where it exists as benzoic acid. Acidic foods and beverages such as fruit juice (citric acid), sparkling drinks (carbonic acid), soft drinks (phosphoric acid), and pickles (vinegar) may be preserved with potassium benzoate.","ru":"Бензоат калия (калийная соль бензойной кислоты) — калиевая соль бензойной кислоты, является консервантом, который подавляет рост плесени, дрожжей и некоторых бактерий. Бензоат калия лучше всего работает в продуктах с низким pH, ниже 4,5, где он существует в виде бензойной кислоты. Химическая формула — K C 7 H 5 O 2 {\\displaystyle \\mathrm {K} C_{7}\\mathrm {H} _{5}\\mathrm {O} _{2}} ."},"fame":31,"pubchemCid":23661960,"mass":160.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)C(=O)[O-].[K+]","inchikey":"XAEFZNCEHLXOMS-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"potassium benzoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"23661960","atoms":15,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.284,"y":-0.166,"z":0.198,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.62,"y":1.057,"z":0.12,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.227,"y":1.09,"z":0.013,"el":"C"},{"x":0.524,"y":-0.096,"z":-0.017,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.164,"y":-1.318,"z":0.062,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.557,"y":-1.354,"z":0.169,"el":"C"},{"x":2.037,"y":-0.059,"z":-0.133,"el":"C"},{"x":2.645,"y":-1.176,"z":-0.154,"el":"O"},{"x":2.586,"y":1.087,"z":-0.2,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.366,"y":-0.192,"z":0.28,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.178,"y":1.98